-- id: exp6966-gguf-load-envelope-canary
-  title: Three-family GGUF load-envelope and teardown canary
-  track: infrastructure
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: claude
-  model: opus
-  requires_gpu: true
-  max_turns: 100
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 240
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.610
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6966_gguf_load_envelope_canary.json
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6962 never reached its learning arms because loading the cached
-    Qwen3.6-35B-A3B GGUF raised no_memory. Both RTX 3090 GPUs were visible and a
-    vocabulary probe passed. V610 needs a task-owned load, generation, teardown,
-    and VRAM-release receipt before any live prompt or learning task runs.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6962_queue_regulated_self_learning.json
-    - {project_root}/scripts/experiments/experiment_6962_queue_regulated_self_learning.py
-    - {project_root}/scripts/experiment_template.py
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/inference/sota_models.py
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/inference/gemma4_quantized.py
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/task_runtime_receipts.py
-    - {project_root}/scripts/run_stop_authority.py
-    - {project_root}/ops/gpu-lease.json and {project_root}/ops/known-issues.md
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/llm-ebm-inference/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Reproduce the Qwen load failure, identify its exact memory and process
-    cause, and prove a bounded sequential runtime for all three mandated GGUF
-    families. Make the smallest safe loader or configuration fix outside
-    scripts/research_conductor.py when the failure is reproducible.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require both NVIDIA devices, no foreign lease owner, all
-       three cached GGUF files, llama.cpp bindings, and a writable checkpoint
-       path. On failure, write blocked_gguf_load_envelope_canary with
-       gate_check_summary. Do not download a replacement quant.
-    1. Add REQ-INFRA-6966 and tests for configuration resolution, subprocess
-       ownership, teardown, and bare gate fields before changing runtime code.
-    2. Declare MODEL_SPECS through cached_sota_pair(gpu_indices=(0, 1)). Require
-       exact hub IDs unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF,
-       unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF, and
-       unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF. Legacy models are smoke-only and cannot
-       set gguf_runtime_ready_score.
-    3. Record baseline GPU memory, processes, model paths, file hashes, GGUF
-       metadata, embedded-tokenizer probe, and the exact Exp6962 load config.
-    4. Reproduce the failing Qwen load once in an owned subprocess. Record the
-       exact exception, allocation request, n_ctx, layer split, mmap/mlock
-       settings, visible devices, and process tree.
-    5. Test a preregistered small configuration ladder. Change one factor at a
-       time. Keep n_ctx at least 16384 for the promoted configuration. Do not
-       use CPU-only execution as the promoted result.
-    6. Load one family at a time. Run one fixed 128-token live generation for
-       each model. Record GPU utilization, offload layers, tokens per second,
-       output hash, and live duration.
-    7. Close the model, end the owned subprocess, run garbage collection, and
-       prove both device memory readings return within 512 MiB of the baseline
-       before loading the next family. Do not kill an unowned process.
-    8. Checkpoint after every model. Set gguf_load_canary_complete_score=1 when
-       all three model rows are terminal. Set gguf_runtime_ready_score=1 only
-       when all three promoted rows used live CUDA, generated nonempty output,
-       exited cleanly, and released memory.
-    9. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,
-       adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
-    10. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific
-        principle per required field and both gguf_load_canary_complete_score
-        and gguf_runtime_ready_score; preconditions_checked;
-        inference_substrate (live_local_llama_cpp_three_family_dual_cuda);
-        duration_s; live_duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; MODEL_SPECS;
-        models_used; model_file_hashes; gpu_topology; baseline_gpu_memory_rows;
-        reproduction_rows; load_config_rows; vocab_probe_rows;
-        live_generation_rows; gpu_runtime_rows; process_ownership_rows;
-        teardown_rows; vram_release_rows; checkpoint_rows;
-        gguf_load_canary_complete_score; gguf_runtime_ready_score; random_seed;
-        reproducibility_checksum; gate_check_summary with failed check,
-        expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict;
-        verifier_is_oracle (false); verdict_class
-        (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);
-        honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6966_gguf_load_envelope_canary.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
-  prior_failures:
-    - experiment_id: exp6962-queue-regulated-self-learning
-      verdict: blocked_queue_regulated_self_learning
-      addressed_by: "This task isolates the no_memory failure, loads one family per owned subprocess, measures the memory ladder, and proves teardown before any learning work."
-      retire_if_same_verdict: true
