-- id: exp6970-bootstrap-prompt-policy-selection
-  title: Bootstrap-stable prompt policy selection
-  track: verification
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 180
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.610
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6970_bootstrap_prompt_policy_selection.json
-  gated_on:
-    - upstream: exp6969-error-structured-prompt-bank
-      artifact_field: prompt_candidate_bank_complete_score
-      op: '=='
-      value: 1
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    ESPO reports that diversity without stable selection can hurt. Exp6969
-    contains only calibration candidates. This task may use calibration exact
-    labels to select one policy. Its result is circular calibration evidence,
-    not a held-out science claim.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6969_error_structured_prompt_bank.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6967_certified_error_headroom_fixture.json
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/experiment_6957_smt_mapping_certification.py
-    - {project_root}/scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-verification/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Certify the 270 calibration candidates. Compare all five policies by model
-    and formulation family. Use a preregistered cluster bootstrap to select one
-    non-baseline policy only when its gain is stable. Seal the selected policy
-    hash for the held-out experiment.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require prompt_candidate_bank_complete_score=1, exactly
-       270 raw rows, the 18 calibration labels, solver witnesses, and no access
-       to held-out labels. On failure, write
-       blocked_bootstrap_prompt_policy_selection with gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-VERIFY-6970 and tests for exact certification, bootstrap seed
-       stability, model-family clustering, tie rules, held-out isolation, and
-       bare gate fields.
-    2. Reparse every raw output. Certify domain cross-feasibility, objective
-       direction, and objective-order preservation with Z3 and bounded
-       enumeration. Keep all malformed, timeout, and unknown rows.
-    3. Compute parse, schema, and exact rates per policy, model, formulation
-       family, and pair. Keep one row for every model, pair, and policy.
-    4. Freeze 2,000 bootstrap resamples clustered by pair and stratified by
-       model and formulation family. Record every resample winner and delta.
-    5. Select a non-baseline policy only if its pooled exact rate exceeds the
-       direct baseline and it wins at least 80% of resamples. Resolve ties by
-       shorter prompt length, then frozen policy ID. Do not tune thresholds.
-    6. Set stable_prompt_policy_ready_score=1 only when a non-baseline policy
-       meets both criteria and all family-specific deltas are reported. Set it
-       to zero for an unstable, tied, or baseline-only result.
-    7. Seal the selected policy text, ID, hash, parser version, bootstrap seed,
-       and calibration source hashes. Do not read or score held-out rows.
-    8. Classify a successful selection as circular_positive because the exact
-       calibration authority selected it. A stable policy still needs Exp6971.
-    9. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,
-       adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
-    10. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific
-        principle per required field and stable_prompt_policy_ready_score;
-        preconditions_checked; inference_substrate
-        (deterministic_exact_calibration_and_cluster_bootstrap);
-        duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; rows; per_candidate_rows;
-        exact_certificate_rows; policy_metric_rows; model_family_rows;
-        formulation_family_rows; bootstrap_rows; bootstrap_winner_rows;
-        calibration_headroom_rows; calibration_delta_over_baseline;
-        selected_policy_id; selected_policy_hash; selected_policy_text_hash;
-        selected_policy_bootstrap_frequency; heldout_isolation_rows;
-        stable_prompt_policy_ready_score; random_seed;
-        reproducibility_checksum; gate_check_summary with failed check,
-        expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict;
-        verifier_is_oracle (true); verdict_class
-        (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);
-        honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6970_bootstrap_prompt_policy_selection.py --date {date}
